        <briefdescription>
<para>Set the position of a point. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Don&apos;t forget that the shape must be convex and the order of points matters. Points should not overlap. This applies to rendering; it is explicitly allowed to temporarily have non-convex or degenerate shapes when not drawn (e.g. during shape initialization).</para>
<para>Point count must be specified beforehand. The behavior is undefined if <computeroutput>index</computeroutput> is greater than or equal to getPointCount.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>index</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Index of the point to change, in range [0 .. <ref refid="classsf_1_1ConvexShape_1a10ab81b7646e7b94c2d0390c99cb67cd" kindref="member">getPointCount()</ref> - 1] </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>point</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>New position of the point</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1ConvexShape_1ae2afef8cb7f19c2d612bb408157b669b" kindref="member">getPoint</ref></computeroutput> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
